## Common Mistakes in Context Engineering

| # | Mistake | Impact | Prevention |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Missing edge cases | Runtime failures in production | Systematic edge case analysis per feature |
| 2 | Weak KPIs (not measurable) | Cannot verify success | Use SMART criteria; include verification method |
| 3 | Undefined scope boundaries | Scope creep during development | Explicit in-scope/out-of-scope tables |
| 4 | Poor acceptance criteria | Ambiguous "done" definition | Link every feature to testable KPIs |
| 5 | No migration plan | Data loss during version upgrade | Plan migration before schema changes |
| 6 | No backward compatibility | v1.0 breaks when v2.0 launches | Additive changes only; migration scripts |
| 7 | No TDD in evolving products | Regression bugs multiply | TDD mandate in Project Boundaries |
| 8 | Role permissions undefined | Security breaches | RBAC document with RLS mapping |
| 9 | No version separation | v1.0 docs overwritten | Separate v1.0 and v2.0 directories |
| 10 | Assumptions undocumented | Surprises during implementation | Explicit assumptions table in Scope |

